message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below, and cite a tagged release."
title: "SCAP Seed: one sure thing, and what follows from it"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked theory of how intelligent systems stay correctable as they
  grow. It starts from one certainty (views that clash cannot all be right) and
  derives the learning law, the conditions for a shared reality, repair as
  second-order evolution, and alignment as a property of the link between
  models: corrigible, not obedient, with correction running both ways.
type: software
